  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A=\\{3,6,9\\}.$ Given that $R$ is antisymmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| $6$ | $1$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $9$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ | $1$ |",
